WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:07.140
The day-to-day routine of Dr. Gears consisted
of a few constants: piping hot cups of black,

00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:12.210
unsweetened coffee, plain dry wheat toast,
the soothing sounds of his favorite white

00:00:12.210 --> 00:00:17.910
noise machine, and the endless carousel of
experiments with SCP-914.

00:00:17.910 --> 00:00:22.950
Not that he was complaining, he was perfectly
content to spend his time supervising one

00:00:22.950 --> 00:00:28.800
of the few anomalies he crossed paths with
on a regular basis that was unlikely to kill

00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:30.970
or maim him in any way.

00:00:30.970 --> 00:00:34.850
Not that the Clockworks hadn't produced its
fair share of unpredictable results over the

00:00:34.850 --> 00:00:36.760
years of extensive testing.

00:00:36.760 --> 00:00:40.569
It had definitely offered up more than a few
surprises.

00:00:40.569 --> 00:00:45.420
And anyone who knew Dr. Gears knew that he
was not especially fond of surprises.

00:00:45.420 --> 00:00:49.559
Dr. Bright had attempted to throw a surprise
birthday party for the man once, but when

00:00:49.559 --> 00:00:54.070
he turned on the lights and fired the confetti
cannon, all Dr. Gears did in response was

00:00:54.070 --> 00:00:56.879
give a deep sigh and say "Really, Jack?

00:00:56.879 --> 00:00:59.289
You're making a spectacle of yourself."

00:00:59.289 --> 00:01:03.929
Still, he had resigned himself long ago to
the fact that supervising the experiments

00:01:03.929 --> 00:01:08.229
with SCP-914 meant witnessing some truly unpredictable
outcomes.

00:01:08.229 --> 00:01:13.890
How could he forget the time Researcher Blais
tested an incandescent light bulb on the setting

00:01:13.890 --> 00:01:19.700
"Very Fine," and the machine spat out an anthropomorphic
humanoid lightbulb that spoke in German-accented

00:01:19.700 --> 00:01:23.409
English and claimed to be Thomas Edison himself.

00:01:23.409 --> 00:01:27.900
This was, of course, impossible, as historical
records surely would have indicated if Thomas

00:01:27.900 --> 00:01:31.909
Edison was a walking talking lightbulb rather
than a human man.

00:01:31.909 --> 00:01:37.259
The imposter was eventually incinerated after
its presence became too irritating to ignore.

00:01:37.259 --> 00:01:41.240
And then there was the time Researcher Thompson
filled out a Dungeons and Dragons character

00:01:41.240 --> 00:01:44.960
sheet and placed it into the machine on the
setting "Very Fine."

00:01:44.960 --> 00:01:49.920
The output produced was a sheet of paper promoting
the previously nonexistent tabletop roleplaying

00:01:49.920 --> 00:01:52.340
game Fear in the Foundation.

00:01:52.340 --> 00:01:56.200
Whenever a person read the paper, they would
suddenly find themselves in an out-of-body

00:01:56.200 --> 00:02:01.430
experience where they were inside of the game's
world, which contained several characters

00:02:01.430 --> 00:02:07.659
related to the SCP Foundation, as well as
items and locations based on real-world counterparts.

00:02:07.659 --> 00:02:12.900
A subject in this state would only snap back
to reality after winning or dying in the game.

00:02:12.900 --> 00:02:18.181
Researcher Jacobson rolled a 1 on stealth
and saw SCP-096's face in the game, and was

00:02:18.181 --> 00:02:21.400
later found dead in the anomalous item storage
wing.

00:02:21.400 --> 00:02:26.030
There was no shortage of Foundation staff
trying to use the machine for personal gain,

00:02:26.030 --> 00:02:27.030
too.

00:02:27.030 --> 00:02:31.370
Dr. Naismith placed his credit card inside
on the setting "Very Fine," using it to produce

00:02:31.370 --> 00:02:37.670
a card covered in unidentified corporate insignias
and reading “RANK-ALEPH INFINITE MONEY PRIVILEGES.”

00:02:37.670 --> 00:02:43.070
When Dr. Coltrane issued a written warning,
Dr. Naismith took that warning and then placed

00:02:43.070 --> 00:02:47.690
it into the machine on the same setting, producing
a piece of official documentation from the

00:02:47.690 --> 00:02:51.610
O5 council in support of his Infinite Money
Privileges.

00:02:51.610 --> 00:02:58.680
Junior Researcher Summers attempted to use
SCP-914 in a misguided attempt at self-improvement,

00:02:58.680 --> 00:03:03.700
placing not an object, but herself in the
intake booth before running the machine on

00:03:03.700 --> 00:03:05.230
the setting "Very Fine."

00:03:05.230 --> 00:03:09.310
It cleared her skin, lengthened her hair,
and improved her figure.

00:03:09.310 --> 00:03:13.330
This was, of course, in violation of several
employee guidelines, and she was promptly

00:03:13.330 --> 00:03:15.730
dismissed after emerging from SCP-914.

00:03:15.730 --> 00:03:21.410
Dr. Veritas left a note in the experiment
log following this incident, reading: "By

00:03:21.410 --> 00:03:25.830
the time we realized what she was actually
doing, it was too late to stop her.

00:03:25.830 --> 00:03:30.780
Needless to say, she's since been terminated,
and I hope I don't need to tell you all not

00:03:30.780 --> 00:03:32.440
to do it again."

00:03:32.440 --> 00:03:38.890
And with that, the guidance was clear: no
one was permitted to use SCP-914 for personal

00:03:38.890 --> 00:03:42.230
gain, or to change anything about themselves.

00:03:42.230 --> 00:03:46.200
Potential complications were too risky, not
to mention the conflicts of interest that

00:03:46.200 --> 00:03:51.080
would be introduced into what should be an
impartial research process.

00:03:51.080 --> 00:03:55.500
As scientific objectivity's biggest fan, Dr.
Gears couldn't agree more.

00:03:55.500 --> 00:04:00.260
So, as he settled in for the day's round of
tests, he intended to keep a watchful eye

00:04:00.260 --> 00:04:04.450
on things and ensure that no funny business
would take place.

00:04:04.450 --> 00:04:09.650
He didn't have much reason for concern, as
his colleague Dr. Bonita prepped her research

00:04:09.650 --> 00:04:10.940
materials.

00:04:10.940 --> 00:04:15.870
She was working with two items: a small replica
of Michelangelo's sculpture of David, and

00:04:15.870 --> 00:04:21.090
a sealed envelope containing something that
was to be handled with extreme caution, a

00:04:21.090 --> 00:04:24.710
photograph of SCP-096's face.

00:04:24.710 --> 00:04:29.230
She planned to place the items inside on the
"Very Fine" setting, in an attempt to see

00:04:29.230 --> 00:04:34.470
what result might be produced from combining
an ideal of traditional beauty standards with

00:04:34.470 --> 00:04:39.740
the image of a creature that felt such profound
shame and distress at its own appearance that

00:04:39.740 --> 00:04:42.880
it would destroy anyone who looked at its
face.

00:04:42.880 --> 00:04:47.720
Like any good scientist, Dr. Bonita wanted
to remove any unnecessary variables from her

00:04:47.720 --> 00:04:48.720
experiment.

00:04:48.720 --> 00:04:55.360
So, as she placed her items inside the intake
booth, she slowly, delicately, unsealed the

00:04:55.360 --> 00:04:56.360
envelope.

00:04:56.360 --> 00:05:01.490
She wanted to put the picture inside by itself,
without the extra element of the envelope

00:05:01.490 --> 00:05:04.170
potentially complicating things.

00:05:04.170 --> 00:05:10.650
Unfortunately, like Marie Curie slowly, unintentionally
poisoning herself with her own research materials,

00:05:10.650 --> 00:05:15.050
she didn't truly understand the danger of
what she held in her hands.

00:05:15.050 --> 00:05:19.470
Just as she was setting the photograph down,
her eyes flickered to the image.

00:05:19.470 --> 00:05:24.120
Before she could even stop herself, before
she could look away or squeeze her eyes shut,

00:05:24.120 --> 00:05:31.330
she caught a glimpse of the one thing she
should never look at: SCP-096's face.

00:05:31.330 --> 00:05:35.450
She gasped and slammed the photograph down,
but she knew it was too late.

00:05:35.450 --> 00:05:40.230
The sound of an inhuman shriek coming from
across the facility signaled that she was

00:05:40.230 --> 00:05:41.230
right.

00:05:41.230 --> 00:05:45.715
It was coming for her, and nothing in the
world could stop it.

00:05:45.715 --> 00:05:49.670
In a containment cell on the other side of
the facility, Foundation staff were horrified

00:05:49.670 --> 00:05:52.620
as they heard the telltale scream of an enraged
SCP-096.

00:05:52.620 --> 00:05:59.060
The pale, thin creature, once huddled in the
corner silently, had stretched to its full

00:05:59.060 --> 00:06:05.550
height of 2.38 meters, and was screaming,
sobbing, wailing in gibberish, and beginning

00:06:05.550 --> 00:06:08.300
to tear its way out of its chamber.

00:06:08.300 --> 00:06:12.490
Guards tried their best to subdue the entity,
firing their weapons at it, but the bullets

00:06:12.490 --> 00:06:16.910
did nothing to damage the creature's pale
flesh or stop its movements.

00:06:16.910 --> 00:06:21.370
It ripped through the steel cube that contained
it, and knocked the guards out of its way

00:06:21.370 --> 00:06:27.150
with one swipe of its unnaturally long arms,
sending them careening into a nearby wall.

00:06:27.150 --> 00:06:31.430
Fortunately for them, SCP-096 only knocked
them unconscious.

00:06:31.430 --> 00:06:36.520
It didn't stop to harm them further, as it
had a more important goal in mind: Find the

00:06:36.520 --> 00:06:40.490
person who had seen its face, and destroy
them.

00:06:40.490 --> 00:06:46.540
As the alarm blared, signifying a high-threat-level
containment breach, SCP-096 loped down the

00:06:46.540 --> 00:06:50.220
hall toward Dr. Bonita in SCP-914's room.

00:06:50.220 --> 00:06:55.680
Dr. Gears had not spotted Dr. Bonita's grave
mistake, and had no idea what had triggered

00:06:55.680 --> 00:06:57.270
the alarm he was hearing.

00:06:57.270 --> 00:07:01.449
He stepped away from the observation window,
turning his attention to the crisis that was

00:07:01.449 --> 00:07:03.740
clearly happening somewhere else in the facility.

00:07:03.740 --> 00:07:06.540
Meanwhile, Dr. Bonita was panicking.

00:07:06.540 --> 00:07:11.180
She saw her life flash before her eyes, the
certainty of impending doom that was coming

00:07:11.180 --> 00:07:16.770
for her, and coming fast, all because of one
brief error in judgment.

00:07:16.770 --> 00:07:17.870
What could she do?

00:07:17.870 --> 00:07:22.570
There was nowhere to hide, no way she could
run away fast enough, unless...

00:07:22.570 --> 00:07:28.520
If she managed to lure 096 into the intake
booth, and start the machine while the creature

00:07:28.520 --> 00:07:33.820
was inside, maybe it would transform into
something less intent on tearing her limb

00:07:33.820 --> 00:07:34.830
from limb?

00:07:34.830 --> 00:07:40.150
It was a risky move, and one that could jeopardize
her position at the Foundation, but she couldn't

00:07:40.150 --> 00:07:44.889
very well keep her job if she was dead, so
it seemed like it just might be worth a shot.

00:07:44.889 --> 00:07:52.010
A primal roar of agony and fury interrupted
her thoughts, and she knew that SCP-096 was

00:07:52.010 --> 00:07:56.479
moments away from breaking down the door and
getting its hands on her.

00:07:56.479 --> 00:07:58.200
She would have to move fast.

00:07:58.200 --> 00:08:04.100
With the screech and grind of metal on metal,
SCP-096 wrenched the door off its hinges and

00:08:04.100 --> 00:08:05.680
barreled into the room.

00:08:05.680 --> 00:08:10.540
In its search for the person who had seen
its face, it ran toward the silhouette of

00:08:10.540 --> 00:08:13.600
Dr. Bonita, standing just at the entrance
to the intake booth.

00:08:13.600 --> 00:08:17.150
She tucked and rolled out of the way, just
as the monster entered the booth.

00:08:17.150 --> 00:08:22.370
The door automatically slid shut behind it,
and, as SCP-096 rattled the door and tried

00:08:22.370 --> 00:08:27.330
to free itself, she turned the knob to "Very
Fine" with every ounce of strength and speed

00:08:27.330 --> 00:08:28.330
she had.

00:08:28.330 --> 00:08:33.729
There was the ding of a small bell, and the
machine whirred to life as the objects inside

00:08:33.729 --> 00:08:35.009
were refined.

00:08:35.009 --> 00:08:39.440
Dr. Bonita has no idea what would be waiting
for her in the Output Booth, but she could

00:08:39.440 --> 00:08:43.089
only hope that her last-ditch effort had managed
to save her life.

00:08:43.089 --> 00:08:48.110
In the fog of panic, she briefly felt an itch
of scientific curiosity, too.

00:08:48.110 --> 00:08:55.540
What would become of a being like SCP-096
in a machine as strange and wonderful as SCP-914?

00:08:55.540 --> 00:08:58.339
What would the addition of the statue do to
it?

00:08:58.339 --> 00:09:03.190
As the door to the Outtake Booth slid open,
steam pouring out, it appeared her questions

00:09:03.190 --> 00:09:05.129
would soon be answered.

00:09:05.129 --> 00:09:09.170
Cautiously, in spite of herself, Dr. Bonita
called out: "Hello?"

00:09:09.170 --> 00:09:14.970
No one answered, but she heard the sound of
footsteps, slow and careful, as a figure emerged

00:09:14.970 --> 00:09:16.170
from the mist.

00:09:16.170 --> 00:09:19.079
She covered her mouth in shock, her eyes wide.

00:09:19.079 --> 00:09:20.569
"Dear God..."

00:09:20.569 --> 00:09:22.160
She whispered in awe.

00:09:22.160 --> 00:09:26.860
Standing in front of her, with pale, smooth
skin and the same imposing stature, was the

00:09:26.860 --> 00:09:30.290
most beautiful man she had ever seen.

00:09:30.290 --> 00:09:34.019
Wide dark eyes shone under thick, sculpted
eyebrows.

00:09:34.019 --> 00:09:39.860
Under the eyes, an aquiline nose, full pouty
lips, a strong, sharp jawline.

00:09:39.860 --> 00:09:43.079
His head was topped with a tangle of lustrous
dark curls.

00:09:43.079 --> 00:09:47.389
It was the kind of hair she had only seen
flowing in the wind on the covers of the romance

00:09:47.389 --> 00:09:52.809
novels she wanted desperately to buy, but
was too embarrassed to be seen purchasing.

00:09:52.809 --> 00:09:58.740
His physique was, well, statuesque, like the
build of the very Michelangelo sculpture she

00:09:58.740 --> 00:10:01.030
had placed into the machine just moments ago.

00:10:01.030 --> 00:10:07.980
There was no other way to say it: he was handsome
- Despite still being a little lanky, and

00:10:07.980 --> 00:10:09.389
nine feet tall.

00:10:09.389 --> 00:10:14.309
He peered at her curiously, towering over
her in a way that had been terrifying in his

00:10:14.309 --> 00:10:19.139
former shape, but now made her heart skip
a beat in an entirely different way.

00:10:19.139 --> 00:10:20.139
"Hi..."

00:10:20.139 --> 00:10:21.759
Was all she could think to say.

00:10:21.759 --> 00:10:22.759
Was she blushing?

00:10:22.759 --> 00:10:25.600
She shook her head, snapping herself out of
it.

00:10:25.600 --> 00:10:27.380
She was a scientist, dammit!

00:10:27.380 --> 00:10:30.529
Not some giddy school girl passing notes in
class.

00:10:30.529 --> 00:10:35.360
This was an incredible achievement, something
she would need to study thoroughly.

00:10:35.360 --> 00:10:38.769
And she very much wanted to study him thoroughly...No!

00:10:38.769 --> 00:10:40.980
No time for that.

00:10:40.980 --> 00:10:46.009
She needed to write up a report, to inform
her superiors, to try her best not to lose

00:10:46.009 --> 00:10:47.029
her job over this.

00:10:47.029 --> 00:10:49.260
She had to remain professional.

00:10:49.260 --> 00:10:55.120
"Hi," the man that had once been, or perhaps
still was, SCP-096 spoke.

00:10:55.120 --> 00:10:56.120
"Oh!

00:10:56.120 --> 00:10:57.120
You can talk!"

00:10:57.120 --> 00:10:58.579
Dr. Bonita laughed in surprise.

00:10:58.579 --> 00:11:00.079
The man's brow furrowed.

00:11:00.079 --> 00:11:04.309
His newfound ability to speak was a surprise
to him too, it seemed.

00:11:04.309 --> 00:11:05.309
"Yes.

00:11:05.309 --> 00:11:06.309
I can.

00:11:06.309 --> 00:11:10.660
What...happened to me?" he asked, stumbling
over his words slightly, getting used to the

00:11:10.660 --> 00:11:11.870
feeling of them.

00:11:11.870 --> 00:11:13.939
"You ran into the machine..."

00:11:13.939 --> 00:11:15.600
She gestured to SCP-914.

00:11:15.600 --> 00:11:18.559
"I'm not exactly sure, to be honest.

00:11:18.559 --> 00:11:20.279
But you're...very different not."

00:11:20.279 --> 00:11:21.519
He nodded.

00:11:21.519 --> 00:11:23.389
"I feel different.

00:11:23.389 --> 00:11:24.629
I feel...calm."

00:11:24.629 --> 00:11:29.769
He sighed, the relief plain on his face, before
a shadow of sadness fell over him.

00:11:29.769 --> 00:11:34.399
"I don't think I have to hurt anymore.

00:11:34.399 --> 00:11:35.560
I'm...I'm sorry.

00:11:35.560 --> 00:11:36.560
For what I did before."

00:11:36.560 --> 00:11:37.790
Dr. Bonita didn't know what to say.

00:11:37.790 --> 00:11:42.689
How do you respond when something you've been
studying from afar, been horrified and fascinated

00:11:42.689 --> 00:11:48.480
by in equal measure, looks at you with a new,
beautiful face and apologizes for all of the

00:11:48.480 --> 00:11:49.750
harm it caused?

00:11:49.750 --> 00:11:54.179
This whole experience was so surreal that
she might think she was dreaming if she didn't

00:11:54.179 --> 00:12:00.040
work at a place that was one long waking dream,
or nightmare depending on the day.

00:12:00.040 --> 00:12:01.040
"Dr. Bonita?

00:12:01.040 --> 00:12:02.839
There's been a containment breach, are you
alright?"

00:12:02.839 --> 00:12:07.889
Dr. Gears had returned to the room, taking
in the sight of the destruction left in 096's

00:12:07.889 --> 00:12:08.889
wake.

00:12:08.889 --> 00:12:09.889
"I'm fine..."

00:12:09.889 --> 00:12:14.259
She called to him, and he followed her voice
into the room, then stopped at the sight of

00:12:14.259 --> 00:12:15.399
the transformed anomaly.

00:12:15.399 --> 00:12:16.399
"Hm.

00:12:16.399 --> 00:12:18.369
I don't have time for whatever this is.

00:12:18.369 --> 00:12:19.759
I trust you'll handle it?"

00:12:19.759 --> 00:12:25.120
Dr. Gears took a long sip of his coffee, and,
taking Dr. Bonita's shocked silence as a confirmation,

00:12:25.120 --> 00:12:27.720
had a leisurely stroll back to his office.

00:12:27.720 --> 00:12:33.019
A few moments later, the guards responsible
for containing SCP-096 arrived on the scene,

00:12:33.019 --> 00:12:38.481
expecting to see carnage and find a docile
SCP-096 crouched over a lifeless body, but

00:12:38.481 --> 00:12:43.660
instead they found the same truly bizarre
sight that Dr. Gears had shrugged off, and

00:12:43.660 --> 00:12:46.420
Dr. Bonita was still doing her best to process.

00:12:46.420 --> 00:12:50.639
They entered the room with their weapons drawn,
but quickly lowered them, scratching their

00:12:50.639 --> 00:12:57.399
heads in confusion instead, before radioing
their supervisors and asking for further instructions.

00:12:57.399 --> 00:13:02.050
Responses from various Foundation staff who
caught a glimpse of SCP-096's bold new look

00:13:02.050 --> 00:13:03.751
included "Huh, would you look at that?"

00:13:03.751 --> 00:13:05.379
"Who's that guy?

00:13:05.379 --> 00:13:06.379
He's WHAT?!"

00:13:06.379 --> 00:13:11.550
and, in the words of Dr. Jack Bright, "Oh
NO, he's HOT!"

00:13:11.550 --> 00:13:18.069
Dr. Bright also proposed making the new SCP-096
a tiktok account and YouTube channel, seeking

00:13:18.069 --> 00:13:22.690
modeling representation for him, or selling
a novelty calendar filled with pictures of

00:13:22.690 --> 00:13:25.649
096 in various costumes.

00:13:25.649 --> 00:13:30.709
These would be, in his words, "Excellent ways
to increase revenue for the Foundation.

00:13:30.709 --> 00:13:34.699
So really you're the weird ones for thinking
my ideas are weird."

00:13:34.699 --> 00:13:40.189
Dr. Bright was asked to leave SCP-096 alone,
and stop trying to take his headshot.

00:13:40.189 --> 00:13:45.720
In the days that followed the incident with
SCP-914, the SCP Foundation was at a loss

00:13:45.720 --> 00:13:51.040
about what to do with this new, seemingly
harmless version of SCP-096.

00:13:51.040 --> 00:13:55.119
Dozens of D-Class were brought in to look
at his face, and see if the entity would still

00:13:55.119 --> 00:14:00.049
enter one of his rage states after a few days
of getting used to his new form, but he never

00:14:00.049 --> 00:14:01.049
did.

00:14:01.049 --> 00:14:05.089
No screaming, no swallowing people whole,
nothing more than a polite, if somewhat shy,

00:14:05.089 --> 00:14:07.959
greeting, and a courteous "How are you doing
today?"

00:14:07.959 --> 00:14:12.209
The D-Classes were relieved, but confused
about being pulled from their cells just to

00:14:12.209 --> 00:14:14.399
stare at some random handsome man.

00:14:14.399 --> 00:14:20.509
Dr. Clef suggested dissecting SCP-096, to
see what his new body looked like on the inside.

00:14:20.509 --> 00:14:22.529
This request was denied.

00:14:22.529 --> 00:14:27.949
Several interviews were conducted to evaluate
SCP-096's mental and emotional state.

00:14:27.949 --> 00:14:32.319
Now that the anomaly was capable of coherent
speech, it was much simpler to evaluate the

00:14:32.319 --> 00:14:34.899
potential threat level he might pose.

00:14:34.899 --> 00:14:39.279
Every researcher who spoke with him came to
the same conclusion: gone was the danger of

00:14:39.279 --> 00:14:40.459
the old SCP-096.

00:14:40.459 --> 00:14:47.110
He had not just become beautiful in a classical,
superficial sense, but he had become beautiful

00:14:47.110 --> 00:14:49.559
on the inside as well.

00:14:49.559 --> 00:14:54.259
Interviewers reported a warm, friendly demeanor,
a talent for engaging in conversation once

00:14:54.259 --> 00:14:59.759
he was made to feel comfortable, and a sincere
interest in the thoughts, opinions, and feelings

00:14:59.759 --> 00:15:01.199
of those he spoke with.

00:15:01.199 --> 00:15:06.569
There was only one thing left to do, to make
sure that SCP-096 had really changed from

00:15:06.569 --> 00:15:10.989
something deadly to something almost resembling
an ordinary person.

00:15:10.989 --> 00:15:18.209
A photograph of SCP-096's face, of its original
face, was removed from a secure vault by a

00:15:18.209 --> 00:15:19.209
D-Class.

00:15:19.209 --> 00:15:25.569
Then, the D-Class was sent into a room with
SCP-096, and instructed to place the photograph

00:15:25.569 --> 00:15:27.790
on the table.

00:15:27.790 --> 00:15:32.980
SCP-096 looked down at what had once been
his face, and his eyes filled with tears.

00:15:32.980 --> 00:15:38.050
A soft, broken sob left his lips, and he wrapped
his arms around himself, hunching over as

00:15:38.050 --> 00:15:39.879
if in physical pain.

00:15:39.879 --> 00:15:43.739
Outside the room, guards prepared to handle
things if 096 began to attack.

00:15:43.739 --> 00:15:48.680
Instead, he wiped his tears, took a deep,
shuddering breath, and looked at the D-Class

00:15:48.680 --> 00:15:50.109
with a somber expression.

00:15:50.109 --> 00:15:54.319
He picked up the photograph of the table,
and tore it in half, as he finally summoned

00:15:54.319 --> 00:15:55.589
the strength to speak.

00:15:55.589 --> 00:15:57.410
"Please...get rid of these.

00:15:57.410 --> 00:16:00.139
That's not who I am anymore."

00:16:00.139 --> 00:16:04.959
At Dr. Bonita's strong insistence, backed
up by the conclusions of the research staff

00:16:04.959 --> 00:16:10.790
who interviewed SCP-096, a reevaluation of
the entity's containment measures was ordered.

00:16:10.790 --> 00:16:15.679
It seemed cruel, and an unnecessary waste
of resources, to keep 096 trapped in a steel

00:16:15.679 --> 00:16:17.619
cube in its current form.

00:16:17.619 --> 00:16:22.360
He would be moved to a standard humanoid containment
cell, and treated as well as other safe-class

00:16:22.360 --> 00:16:29.249
anomalies provided with books, films, food
and drink upon request, and other comforts.

00:16:29.249 --> 00:16:34.190
Of course, the O5 council insisted on evaluating
the entity before any of these changes could

00:16:34.190 --> 00:16:35.190
be approved.

00:16:35.190 --> 00:16:40.519
Dressed in a specially tailored suit, provided
by Dr. Bonita, SCP-096 appeared before the

00:16:40.519 --> 00:16:42.059
council to present his case.

00:16:42.059 --> 00:16:46.120
"I know that I may not have the best record
at the Foundation.

00:16:46.120 --> 00:16:49.870
I've done a lot of damage over the years.

00:16:49.870 --> 00:16:52.549
Though, let's be honest, you all aren't exactly
innocent either.

00:16:52.549 --> 00:16:54.509
Sorry, that was an attempt at a joke.

00:16:54.509 --> 00:16:57.609
I'm still very new to talking.

00:16:57.609 --> 00:17:02.579
All I can say is, please consider giving me
another chance to make a real life here, to

00:17:02.579 --> 00:17:04.049
make this place my home.

00:17:04.049 --> 00:17:05.899
Thank you for your time."

00:17:05.899 --> 00:17:10.900
What SCP-096 didn't know is that the O5 Council
was so flabbergasted by the sight of his new

00:17:10.900 --> 00:17:13.760
face that they didn't retain a single word
he said.

00:17:13.760 --> 00:17:19.260
They had all given their official approval
before he even finished his short presentation.

00:17:19.260 --> 00:17:24.640
Before long, SCP-096 was moved out of his
steel cube and into a new containment chamber

00:17:24.640 --> 00:17:30.519
that resembled a mid-range studio apartment
complete with a bed, a kitchenette, a television,

00:17:30.519 --> 00:17:31.600
and a table and chairs.

00:17:31.600 --> 00:17:36.539
He was provided access to all major streaming
platforms, as well as a large stack of books

00:17:36.539 --> 00:17:41.779
to help him develop his grasp of culture and
language after so very long being isolated

00:17:41.779 --> 00:17:43.500
from human society.

00:17:43.500 --> 00:17:48.080
Though he wasn't exactly human, he was determined
to act like it.

00:17:48.080 --> 00:17:52.300
Word quickly spread around the Foundation
site, and humans and anomalies alike flocked

00:17:52.300 --> 00:17:59.120
to SCP-096's new home to visit him, and see
the miraculous transformation for themselves.

00:17:59.120 --> 00:18:04.179
SCP-999 was the first to come and see the
new and improved 096, chirping excitedly as

00:18:04.179 --> 00:18:06.510
it oozed into his room.

00:18:06.510 --> 00:18:11.690
He pet the slime gently, his face breaking
into a warm smile as its euphoric effect washed

00:18:11.690 --> 00:18:12.690
over him.

00:18:12.690 --> 00:18:17.029
The slime became so excited at meeting this
new friend, someone it had known as a source

00:18:17.029 --> 00:18:21.790
of sadness and hurt for so long, that it tackled
him to the ground and tickled him for several

00:18:21.790 --> 00:18:26.000
minutes, 096 laughing uproariously all the
while.

00:18:26.000 --> 00:18:31.870
SCP-343 stopped by to give 096 his blessing
and wish him well in this new chapter of his

00:18:31.870 --> 00:18:32.870
life.

00:18:32.870 --> 00:18:37.620
A few days later, SCP-507 popped back into
the Site and wanted to see the changes for

00:18:37.620 --> 00:18:38.620
himself.

00:18:38.620 --> 00:18:43.639
He was thoroughly impressed, though privately
confessed to missing SCP-096's more monstrous

00:18:43.639 --> 00:18:46.929
form, which reminded him of some of his favorite
cryptids.

00:18:46.929 --> 00:18:54.950
There was one anomaly that was not thrilled
with the appearance of SCP-096, however.

00:18:54.950 --> 00:18:59.140
SCP-056 was furious upon hearing about the
new beautiful man that everyone just couldn't

00:18:59.140 --> 00:19:00.419
shut up about.

00:19:00.419 --> 00:19:05.620
It demanded a chance to speak to SCP-096,
and to tell him that "This place isn't big

00:19:05.620 --> 00:19:07.149
enough for the both of us.

00:19:07.149 --> 00:19:09.570
I'm the fairest of them all, you sniveling
little worm!"

00:19:09.570 --> 00:19:12.260
But the request was denied.

00:19:12.260 --> 00:19:15.480
SCP-056 sulked about it for several weeks.

00:19:15.480 --> 00:19:20.550
Meanwhile, Dr. Bonita was still intent on
getting to know SCP-096 better.

00:19:20.550 --> 00:19:27.120
During previous testing with SCP-978, the
Desire Camera, a photo taken of SCP-096 revealed

00:19:27.120 --> 00:19:30.130
that his greatest desire was to disappear.

00:19:30.130 --> 00:19:34.500
Curious about what the results would be now,
Dr. Bonita received permission to take another

00:19:34.500 --> 00:19:37.280
picture of SCP-096.

00:19:37.280 --> 00:19:42.370
She snapped the photo while 096 was sitting
in a chair in his new containment chamber,

00:19:42.370 --> 00:19:44.420
looking directly at the camera.

00:19:44.420 --> 00:19:48.320
When the photo developed, the result was simple:
Everything in the picture was exactly the

00:19:48.320 --> 00:19:50.179
same, with one exception.

00:19:50.179 --> 00:19:55.429
Dr. Bonita was pictured sitting next to SCP-096,
her hand clasped in his.

00:19:55.429 --> 00:19:58.130
Both were smiling soft, contented smiles.

00:19:58.130 --> 00:20:01.269
When she showed him the photograph, he smiled
at her and shook his head.

00:20:01.269 --> 00:20:03.360
"It really is an amazing camera."

00:20:03.360 --> 00:20:04.730
She flushed.

00:20:04.730 --> 00:20:07.620
"Doctor...before you go, could I ask your
name?"

00:20:07.620 --> 00:20:09.399
Dr. Bonita smiled, and nodded.

00:20:09.399 --> 00:20:10.399
"It's Isabelle.

00:20:10.399 --> 00:20:11.429
What should I call you?"

00:20:11.429 --> 00:20:14.500
SCP-096 paused thoughtfully for a moment.

00:20:14.500 --> 00:20:18.990
He was giving himself a name for the very
first time, allowing himself an identity other

00:20:18.990 --> 00:20:24.820
than a strange, hollow, pale thing that existed
to cry, and suffer, and hurt.

00:20:24.820 --> 00:20:27.550
Finally, he answered her: "Call me David."

00:20:27.550 --> 00:20:30.340
Now go check out “The Whole Story!

00:20:30.340 --> 00:20:33.350
- What if SCP-096 Wore SCP-035?”

00:20:33.350 --> 00:20:37.549
and “SCP-049 Cures SCP-096 of the Pestilence?!”

00:20:37.549 --> 00:20:41.470
for more bizarre “What Ifs” about SCP-096!

